+// The list span sets the item's block font; spans are applied in priority
+// order, so giving it a higher priority applies it first and lets inline styles
+// inside the item (code, strong, …) override it. Set later at equal priority,
+// it replaced them: inline code in a list lost its monospace font.
+private const val LIST_SPAN_FLAGS = SPAN_FLAGS_EXCLUSIVE_EXCLUSIVE or (1 shl Spanned.SPAN_PRIORITY_SHIFT)
